      "tactic_notes": "<p>Eberon, the Defiler has 3 action per round.</p>\n<p>Each round it will attack once for each of his <strong>Claw</strong>, <strong>Tail </strong>and <strong>Wing </strong>attack. For its tail attack, he will rotate between its<strong> Tail Stab</strong> and <strong>Tail Slam</strong>, regardless if there is a <strong>Grappled </strong>creature or not.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Eberon will only use the rest of its attacks on its fight at the top of the mountain.</p>\n<p>It will starts the fight in its Umbral Armored form and replace one of its basic attack with <strong>Ebon Breath</strong> attack. Replace any attack as see fit but the <strong>Ebon Breath</strong> will always be the last attack of each round. If its ation is reduced in any way, remove one of its basic attack and keep using the <strong>Ebon Breath</strong>.</p>\n<p>On the last turn of its<strong> Ebon Armor</strong> form, it will replace <strong>Ebon Breath</strong> with <strong>Darkfire Eruption</strong>.</p>\n<p>Eberon will use its <strong>Umbral Infused </strong>once after it enters <strong>Crisis </strong>and is NOT in its <strong>Umbral Armor</strong> form.</p>\n<p>If its Zero Power Clock is full, it will use its Zero Power with its next action.</p>",
